                <pb facs="0786" n="726" xml:id="pg726"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Señor Benitez to Mr. Washburn.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of State for Foreign
                                affairs,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Luque,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 20, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Portuguese subject, Don José Maria Leite Pereira, having disappeared some
                    days since from his ordinary residence in Trinidad, in contravention of orders
                    in force, I have the honor to inquire of your excellency if it be true, as the
                    police has been informed, that the said individual is now in the American
                    legation, and for how long since; hoping your excellency will also please inform
                    me of the nature and motive of his remaining in that legation.</p>
                <p>At the same time I beg your excellency will remit me a list of all the persons
                    who, without belonging to the legation, are sheltered in it.</p>
                <p>On this occasion I have the honor to renew to your excellency the assurances of
                    my most distinguished consideration and esteem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GUMESINDO BENITEZ.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles A. Washburn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of
                            America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
